  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Rehabilitation and Expansion of Tea Production (COTHEGAB)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">COTHEGAB is a cooperative of tea growers in Nyamagabe District; they have a total membership of 1,766 members of whom 298 female members. COTHEGAB have a big demand for green tea leaves from the nearby Mushubi Tea Company (MTC) factory; they wish to increase productivity as one way to increase production quantities; but they wish also to expand to new plantations and also fill gaps in existing plantations. The grant will help them address these issues, namely setting up of a nursery (MTC will contribute), building a storage for fertilizer so as to have enough and timely, fertilizer purchase fund, transport means: truck so as to transport the tea leaves in the best conditions and reach the factory on time, and motorcycles for agronomists to enable them reach all farmers easily and provide efficient and timely extension services, training of farmers.</narrative>
  </description>
